        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the inpatient treatment of your 72-year-old female patient, admitted on 29/05/2022 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia, chest X-ray showing pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout the stay. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. Treatment consisted of controlled oxygen therapy, inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. She is discharged in stable condition and I recommend close follow-up including spirometry assessment. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
